analysisWe need map. Given only three atomic facts, likely all apply to many elements. F001 lists applicants – needed for scope, interference, etc. F002 complaint about disproportionate measures – relevant to interference, prescribed by law, legitimate aim, necessity, positive obligation. F003 other complaints – maybe not needed. We'll assign.

Scope needs existence of assembly and participation -> F001 gives applicants details; maybe also F002 indicates they were organizers/participants. So both F001,F002.

Interference: need claim of measures -> F002.

Prescribed by law: need law basis – not in given facts, but maybe none => empty list.

Legitimate aim: need justification – not present -> empty.

Necessity: need proportionality – not present -> empty.

Positive obligation: maybe derived from jurisprudence but not factual -> empty.

